          "path": "_m/u/1/7/e/hoorn-wp/het-spectrum-vanaf-boven.jpg",
          "filename": "Het Spectrum vanaf boven..jpg",
          "caption": "The kindergarten building has been made yellow, the BSO building red and the building for the superstructure green.Google Lens AI overview   Confirm AI answers independently if possible \nThis aerial image shows the campus of Oecumenische Basisschool Het Spectrum, located at Volkerakweg 1 in Hoorn, North Holland.\nBased on your color-coded highlights and the school's layout:\nYellow: The curved building is the main school facility, primarily housing the kindergarten (lower school) classes.\nBlue (Red request): This rectangular building next to the playground serves as the BSO (Buitenschoolse Opvang) or after-school care facility.\nGreen: This building across the street (Breitnerhof) is the location for the superstructure (bovenbouw) groups.\n\nThe school is part of the Penta foundation and serves roughly 311 students across these closely situated buildings in the Kersenboogerd district.",
          "alt": "The kindergarten building has been made yellow, the BSO building red and the building for the superstructure green.Google Lens AI overview   Confirm AI answers independently if possible \nThis aerial image shows the campus of Oecumenische Basisschool Het Spectrum, located at Volkerakweg 1 in Hoorn, North Holland.\nBased on your color-coded highlights and the school's layout:\nYellow: The curved building is the main school facility, primarily housing the kindergarten (lower school) classes.\nBlue (Red request): This rectangular building next to the playground serves as the BSO (Buitenschoolse Opvang) or after-school care facility.\nGreen: This building across the street (Breitnerhof) is the location for the superstructure (bovenbouw) groups.\n\nThe school is part of the Penta foundation and serves roughly 311 students across these closely situated buildings in the Kersenboogerd district.",
